@startuml donor-lifecycle
' Revision 2026-10-13: wave-5 zero-egress admission, R-TRANSFER and controlled verification; formats/qualification unpublished.
' Revision 2026-10-12: R-OPERATOR operator custody and lifecycle acts; R-WORKPLACE service controls, helper-v1 activation and execution-level stops; Draft, no renderer/qualification evidence.
title Donor lifecycle - Draft target A first / B disabled / C fallback; four independent descriptive axes, no closed state schema
state "Donor installation\nowner: donor / bridge role; B separate provisioner pending" as Installation {
  state "Present\nvariant-owned service, config, keys, home" as Present
  state "Purged\nlocal owned artifacts removed; donor audit retained" as Purged
  Present --> Purged : human purge: stop owned processes; A/C preserve donor account;
  Present --> Purged : B removal requires separate specified provisioner; B currently disabled
}
state "Donor execution\nowner: bridge-role supervisor\nA/C donor UID; B bridge UID" as Execution {
  state "Active\nqualified lockdown + remote-auto; current generation" as Active
  state "Stopped\npersisted stop mark; bridge and keys kept" as Stopped
  state "Left\nchannel closed; keys/config kept" as Left
  state "Refused run / rejoin outcome\nprior persistent execution state retained\nno fallback posture or identity" as Refused
  Active --> Stopped : human stop: persist first, terminate only owned harness/descendants
  Active --> Left : human leave: request retirement when reachable; close channel
  Stopped --> Left : human leave; retain identity
  Stopped --> Active : human run; admission, credentials and exact qualification remain valid
  Stopped --> Refused : absent/invalid admission, credential, tuple or current policy
  Left --> Stopped : human init --rejoin; new invitation/package and newly admitted workplace; wait for run
  Left --> Refused : revoked identity / invalid admission or qualification
}
state "Project workplace\nowner: swarma-operator (no harness) + dispatcher/helper + project bridge\nhelper root boundary; workplace UID jobs only\nservice-principal executor owns policy/claims/audit/mailbox" as Workplace {
  state "Admitted workplace\nqualified zero egress / exec profile / host matrix; fixed relay shell" as Admitted
  state "Suspended\ngrants paused; sessions closed; workplace kept" as Suspended
  state "Retirement in progress\nrevocation persisted before termination/restart" as Retiring
  state "Retired\nquiesce + declared-key cleanup; delete home; account/egress released" as Retired
  Admitted --> Suspended : operator suspend / R-WATCH one-account freeze + journaled stop / R-ALLSTOP
  Admitted --> Retiring : operator retire; stop user-cert renewal, user KRL, close sessions
  Suspended --> Retiring : operator retire
  Retiring --> Retired : journaled exec.stop; account-wide absence/fence + recorded export or operator waiver + key cleanup/home deletion
}
state "Worker signing identity / three pinned keys\nowner: operator-authorized trust registry / key keeper\nprivate keys remain on donor" as Identity {
  state "Pinned\nretirement and leave preserve identity" as Pinned
  state "Revoked\nold frames/envelopes refused" as Revoked
  Pinned --> Revoked : separate operator-authorized root-signed revoke of K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh
}
note right of Installation
  Purge may happen offline; remote retirement/revocation then UNKNOWN.
  No transition from local purge to project retirement or identity revoke.
  A removes user service/artifacts; C also removes sandbox artifacts.
  B allocated accounts/egress/sandbox/system service: removal spec pending.
end note
note right of Execution
  Named run/rejoin arrows describe validated return, not automatic restart.
  Project cannot prevent donor stop/leave/purge.
  Project watcher/all-stop uses existing channel-down behaviour: pause new turns,
  current deadline then park; explicit recovery, no new donor state.
end note
note right of Workplace
  R-OPERATOR operator acts: phone main with secure-element operator device key,
  biometric exact-act signature; pinned-key SSH over tailnet, forced operator command/no shell.
  Terminal fallback: password sudo, timestamp_timeout=0, no NOPASSWD.
  Widening authenticates + confirms and refuses agent sessions; standing retirement
  and explicit home retention are in the owner widening list. Narrowing authenticates only;
  phone revocation: one biometric confirmation. Reads: swarma-observer, no confirmation.
  Formats and phone-key lifecycle unpublished; existing signed domains unchanged.
  [[../CIP-0011-credential-broker-and-agent-users.md#5-curator-broker R-OPERATOR authority boundary]]
  Per-job or standing-runner execution shape/concurrency/blast radius unpublished.
  Process-group death alone proves no execution absence.
  Failure to prove process absence cannot authorize account release.
  Retirement forward-recovery states/record encoding
  unspecified in spec CIP-0009 D7; no invented retry state machine.
  Project suspension resume grammar unspecified in spec CIP-0009 D7.
end note
note right of Identity
  Revoke stops renewal, updates user KRL and closes established sessions.
  R-TRANSFER code export or operator waiver precedes home deletion.
  Retirement metadata alone is service-generated closed-schema data,
  with no agent-controlled strings, names, links or bodies. Separate explicit
  operator home retention states confidentiality is not guaranteed.
  Certificate revocation alone does not stop an existing connection.
  Return after revoke requires new keys through new enrollment.
  Dispatcher one-shot identity exception never applies to donor identity.
  [[../CIP-0009-donor-side-deployment-and-bridge.md#recommendation CIP-0009 D7/D12]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#tools-mailbox-and-lifecycle Lifecycle contract]]
end note
note bottom of Workplace
  R-ALLSTOP manual narrowing act: phone auth + one confirmation or terminal fallback;
  refused inside agent sessions; hold/range deny/all generations journaled absence,
  broker freeze (delivered tokens retain vendor lifetime), host closes delivery/snapshots.
  Partial/unknown keeps admission closed; each service journals; explicit recovery only.
  R-WATCH read-only least-privileged per-UID sampler; hard threshold narrows one account;
  phone alerts, no unjournaled kill. Formats/thresholds unpublished.
  Standing workplace allowed; loop at donor only. Trusted standing surfaces digest checked.
  R-TRANSFER each round: fresh B/C materialization, fence/absence/export, exact board review.
end note
@enduml
